      "claim_refs": ["CL07"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "The headline number",
      "narration": "In donor pair 1, the lean-donor recipients gained 24% less fat mass than the obese-donor recipients, p equals 0.003.",
      "on_screen": "Bar pair labelled 'Donor pair 1 (main text)' with '24% less fat mass gain, p = 0.003' called out",
      "claim_refs": ["CL01"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "One of four donor pairs",
      "narration": "But that is one of four donor pairs. Pair 2 was minus 6%, p equals 0.41; pair 3 was plus 3%, p equals 0.72; pair 4 was minus 19%, p equals 0.04.",
      "on_screen": "Four-row table of donor pairs with effect and p-value: 1, -24%, p = 0.003; 2, -6%, p = 0.41; 3, +3%, p = 0.72; 4, -19%, p = 0.04; footer 'supplementary materials, S3'",
      "claim_refs": ["CL02"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "Pooled across pairs",
      "narration": "Pooled across the four pairs the difference was minus 11%, 95% confidence interval minus 23% to plus 1% - an interval that does not exclude no effect.",
      "on_screen": "Forest-style plot: pooled point at -11% with 95% CI -23% to +1% crossing the zero line",
      "claim_refs": ["CL03"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "The food-intake control",
      "narration": "And in the pair-fed arm, where food intake was equalised, the difference was minus 4%, p equals 0.55. The record says a substantial part of the main-text effect is attributable to differences in food intake rather than to the transferred microbiota.",
      "on_screen": "Side-by-side: 'Main text (intake not equalised)' vs 'Pair-fed, diet-matched arm: -4%, p = 0.55'; caption 'supplementary materials, S2'",
      "claim_refs": ["CL04", "CL05"]
